{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"AC5 SATISFIED — PR #131 is CLOSED.\n\n  gh pr view 131 --repo navapbc/rebar --json state,closed,closedAt\n  -> {\"state\": \"CLOSED\", \"closed\": true, \"closedAt\": \"2026-08-20T04:02:53Z\"}\n\nSequence, verified rather than assumed:\n  03:55:43Z  Gerrit 1943 submitted, MERGED as dab851c5fb53db4e2cd63e49a305997e4db48f3b\n  ~04:0xZ    GitHub mirror refs/heads/main advanced to dab851c5fb (polled until confirmed)\n  04:02:53Z  dependabot auto-closed #131, with the comment:\n             'Looks like these dependencies are no longer updatable, so this is no longer needed.'\n\nThat closing reason is the direct consequence of taking the current resolution instead of the PR's stale pins: with botocore at 1.43.75, genai-prices at 0.1.4 and json-repair at 0.63.3 on main, dependabot had nothing left to propose. Had the lock been pinned back to 1.43.72 / 0.1.3 / 0.63.2, dependabot would instead have opened a fresh PR for the remaining patches.\n\nManual-close fallback was NOT needed, but the cross-reference was still posted so nobody re-analyses this PR later:\n  https://github.com/navapbc/rebar/pull/131#issuecomment-5351206840\nnaming Gerrit 1943, merged sha dab851c5fb, and the per-package proposed-vs-landed table.\n\nAll five acceptance criteria are met. Closing."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787198643347453001,"uuid":"05753d85-97d9-46cf-b751-5bc32084fabb"}